Experimental Design for a Paper

Now that we have an idea of what we could learn, here’s an outline for a possible academic study:

1. Baseline: Visualizing a Transformer Before Training
	•	PCA plots of word embeddings before learning.
	•	Heatmaps of random self-attention.
	•	Softmax output distributions before learning.

2. Training on a Tiny Corpus
	•	A dataset of simple English sentences (or math-based questions if we test reasoning).
	•	Train in stages, stopping at different points to analyze learning.

3. Tracking Learning in the Latent Space
	•	Run PCA, t-SNE, or UMAP at each epoch to track how embeddings cluster over time.
	•	Observe if attention follows structured learning or chaotic adaptation.

4. Mathematical Analysis of Learning
	•	Do embedding trajectories align with geometric transformations?
	•	Can we predict how an embedding will move before it learns?

5. Novel Findings
	•	Are there fundamental rules for how transformers learn?
	•	Are attention heads assigned to specific tasks without direct supervision